      "card_ids": ["C19"],
      "claim": "In mice, BPA was reported to pass the BBB with brain boron concentrations comparable to muscle, indicating some CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "Most transferred direct in-vivo CNS exposure records show absent or very low brain/CSF uptake, including CSF below detection, brain/plasma ratio of 0.001, and no detectable brain radioactivity. One high-score record shows BBB passage, but the overall experimental record supports insufficient meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "The single positive BBB-passage record lacks a quantitative brain/plasma ratio or therapeutic relevance threshold.",
    "Transferred negative records span different chemical scaffolds, species, and assays, so applicability to the query is inferred only from assay-transfer scores."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

